* CABSRT10 - RATED USAGE SORT FOR BILL DETAIL ASSEMBLY
* MVT OS/360 SORT/MERGE FORM OF JCL/CTLCARDS/CABSRT10.
* SORTS TELCABS.CABS.RATED.JUR INTO BAN / BILL PERIOD / SECTION /
* LINE SEQUENCE / ELEMENT SEQUENCE ORDER.  CABBIL02 ASSUMES THIS
* ORDER AND DOES NOT VERIFY IT - AN UNSORTED INPUT PRODUCES ONE
* DETAIL LINE PER ELEMENT INSTEAD OF ONE PER GROUP AND THE BILL
* STILL ADDS UP, SO NOTHING DOWNSTREAM CATCHES IT.
*
* THE RULE THAT LEFT THIS CARD
*   THE SUM FIELDS OPERAND ON THE PACKED QUANTITY AT 37 AND THE
*   PACKED AMOUNT AT 45 IS NOT CODED HERE.  THIS SORT HAS NO SUM
*   STATEMENT.  THE E35 EXIT CABSXDTL NOW COLLAPSES TWO RATED
*   RECORDS THAT CARRY THE SAME BAN, PERIOD, SECTION, LINE
*   SEQUENCE AND ELEMENT SEQUENCE INTO ONE AND ADDS THE QUANTITY
*   AND THE AMOUNT.  THAT DEDUPLICATION RULE EXISTS ONLY IN THAT
*   MODULE.  NO COBOL PROGRAM IN THE ESTATE KNOWS THAT DUPLICATE
*   ELEMENT SEQUENCES ARE POSSIBLE.
*
* OPTION EQUALS IS NOT CODED - THIS SORT HAS NO OPTION
* STATEMENT.  CABSXDTL HOLDS THE FIRST RECORD OF EACH GROUP AND
* ADDS THE LATER ONES INTO IT, SO THE SURVIVING RECORD IS THE
* ONE THAT REACHED THE EXIT FIRST WHATEVER ORDER EQUAL KEYS
* LEAVE THE MERGE IN.
*
* THE DEDUPLICATION IS NO LONGER READABLE FROM THIS CONTROL
* CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(1,13,CH,A,14,6,CH,A,20,2,CH,A,22,4,PD,A,35,2,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=(200)
 MODS E35=(CABSXDTL,8192,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
